  "body": "Hi,\n\nI think there was some misunderstanding. The unversioned \"SMART\" dir is NOT supposed to be found directly. The script searches for SMART.exe either directly under the user-specified directory, or in the directory matching the pattern contained in the distributed archive.\n\nDoes the original script still work if you set, in the \"user settings\" section,\n\n```\n$SmartRoot = \"C:\\Users\\My User\\AppData\\Local\\SMART\"\n```\n\ni.e., the directory which directly contains the \"SMART.exe\" program?\n\nOr, equivalently:\n```\n$SmartRoot = Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA \"SMART\"\n```",
